Title: Harrow Creek
Credit: Written by
Author: Example Writer

INT. HARROW CREEK MOTEL - OFFICE - NIGHT

A cramped office. A space heater ticks in the corner. MR. HALE (70s) watches a muted television.

The door opens. MARA (30s), soaked, steps inside.

MR. HALE
Room four. Heater works if you kick it.

MARA
(dripping)
Do you get many visitors this time of year?

MR. HALE
Only the ones looking for something.

He slides a key across the counter.

CUT TO:

EXT. COAST ROAD - DAY

A car rattles north. The pavement ends. A white lighthouse rises from the fog.

AMES (V.O.)
Well. That's new.
